<title>USA: Bristol-Myers to sell off some businesses.</title>
<headline>Bristol-Myers to sell off some businesses.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bristol-Myers Squibb Co said Wednesday said it plans to sell the arthroscopy and surgical instruments businesses of its Zimmer division.</p>
<p>The products are produced by Zimmer's Linvatec and Hall Surgical business units, headquartered in Largo, Florida, the company said in a press release.</p>
<p>The sale will allow Zimmer to focus on its core businesses of hip and knee implants and fracture fixation devices, the company said.</p>
